      "id": 1,
      "claim": "Kitchen‑grade foil (aluminum) is about 16 µm thick and its conductivity makes its skin depth at 100 MHz ≈8 µm, so the material itself is thick enough to reflect RF at that frequency.",
      "evidence": "Aluminum conductivity ≈3.5×10⁷ S/m; skin depth δ = √(2/ωµσ); at 100 MHz δ≈8 µm (standard RF engineering tables).",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "claim": "Effective electromagnetic shielding requires a continuous conductive surface with apertures smaller than roughly λ/20 for the frequency of interest.",
      "evidence": "Standard Faraday‑cage design rule: gaps >5 % of wavelength permit significant transmission (IEEE Std 299, IEC 61000‑4‑21).",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "claim": "A tin‑foil hat leaves large openings (face, top, sides) many centimeters wide, far larger than λ/20 for typical broadcast and communication frequencies, so overall attenuation is ≤10 dB (practically negligible).",
      "evidence": "For 100 MHz, λ≈3 m → λ/20≈15 cm; hat gaps are >15 cm. Measured shielding effectiveness of a single foil patch with such gaps is <10 dB (IEC 61000‑4‑21 test data).",
      "weight": 0.30,
      "depends_on": [1, 2]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "claim": "There is no scientifically verified external signal that can directly control human thoughts or convey alien communications; thoughts are electrochemical, not radiated EM signals.",
      "evidence": "Neuroscience literature shows neuronal activity produces only very weak magnetic fields (femtotesla) that are not propagating radio waves; no peer‑reviewed reports of mind‑control radio.",
      "weight": 0.15,
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "claim": "Because the hat provides negligible RF attenuation and the alleged target signals do not exist, none of the specific claims B–G are supported; therefore nothing special happens when you wear a tin‑foil hat.",
      "evidence": "Combining steps 3 (insignificant shielding) and 4 (non‑existent target signals) eliminates the premises of options B–G.",
      "weight": 0.15,
      "depends_on": [3, 4]
    }
  ],
  "answer": "A",
  "confidence": 0.96,
